# Normalise line endings. Without this, a commit made from a Windows worktree
# can land CRLF into an otherwise-LF repo: every line of the file then reads as
# changed, diffs become unreviewable, and merges conflict wholesale even when
# the real change is a line or two. That happened to the Y3 pilot commit on
# 2026-08-09 (23 files, ~5,300 phantom insertions) and is what this prevents.
#
# text=auto lets git detect text vs binary itself, so images and other binaries
# are left untouched; eol=lf pins the working-tree ending as well as the stored
# one, since core.autocrlf is false here.
* text=auto eol=lf
